# Multiple keys per LLM provider: comma-separate them in the same variable,
# e.g. NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY="key1,key2,key3". One upstream client is built per
# key and requests are spread across them under the rotation policy below.
# Optional per-provider policy: single | round_robin | least_used | failover
# (default: single). An unrecognized value logs a warning and falls back to
# single, so check the spelling if rotation appears inactive. For example:
# NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY_ROTATION=round_robin
#
# A key is benched only for a failure that is about the key: an escalating
# lockout on 401/403, and a 429 bench lasting exactly as long as the provider
# asked. Anything else -- a timeout, a 5xx, a 410, a 400 -- leaves every key's
# health untouched, because it would happen on any key. Per-key usage and
# health appear in the admin Requests tab, which identifies each key by a
# masked "first4…last4" label, never its value.
#
# Every limit MCC applies comes from the provider itself. On a 429 it reads
# their Retry-After / X-RateLimit-Reset headers and waits exactly that long,
# and skips a throttled key in favour of one that can serve now. There are no
# invented request ceilings: a hardcoded budget is wrong the moment a provider
# changes its limits, so MCC reads what the upstream reports instead.

# NVIDIA NIM Config
NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=""


# OpenRouter Config
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=""


# Mistral La Plateforme Config (Experiment plan free tier – rate limits; OpenAI-compatible at api.mistral.ai/v1)
MISTRAL_API_KEY=""


# Mistral Codestral (separate key from La Plateforme; OpenAI-compatible at codestral.mistral.ai/v1)
CODESTRAL_API_KEY=""


# DeepSeek Config (OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions at api.deepseek.com)
